From 46ba507e0450e2070b55ed79d8310732cb779860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jagpal Singh Gill <paligill@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:41:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fw-update: report Software.Update events

The firmware update flow reported progress and failures to the journal
only. Commit the xyz.openbmc_project.Software.Update events[1] instead,
which phosphor-logging maps on to the Redfish Update message registry.

Scope is limited to single device/component updates, driven through the
Software.Update interface of ItemUpdateManager, and to the event set
defined in [1].

Tested:
Unit tests pass, including the new events_test, which drives every
generator against a stand-in phosphor-logging service and checks the
committed event name, TARGET_NAME and IMAGE_IDENTIFIER.

    $ meson test -C builddir
    Ok:                 37
    Fail:               0

Deployed on a Yosemite4, driving a firmware update of a Sentinel Dome
BIC over MCTP.

[1] https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.events.yaml

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/94762]

Change-Id: I4d2753e1d8eb826fb9e9f528ce2f780da4e7994b
Signed-off-by: Jagpal Singh Gill <paligill@gmail.com>
